{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1722"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge history/medieval","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/history__medieval.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",406],["+","Under Charles Martel's protection the Anglo-Saxon missionary Boniface preached to the pagan peoples east of the Rhine. At Geismar near Fritzlar in Hesse, probably around 723, he felled a mighty oak sacred to the thunder god Donar (Thor) to show that the old gods were powerless; when no lightning struck him, many onlookers accepted baptism, and from the timber he built a chapel dedicated to Saint Peter. "],["=",661]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",378],["+","Unter dem Schutz Karl Martells predigte der angelsächsische Missionar Bonifatius den heidnischen Völkern östlich des Rheins. In Geismar bei Fritzlar in Hessen fällte er, wohl um 723, eine mächtige Eiche, die dem Donnergott Donar geweiht war, um die Ohnmacht der alten Götter zu beweisen; als ihn kein Blitz traf, ließen sich viele Zuschauer taufen, und aus dem Holz baute er eine dem heiligen Petrus geweihte Kapelle. "],["=",635]]}]},
